  "llm_reasoning_text": "\n## Index Recommendation Summary\n\nAll indexes were validated using estimate_index_cost before recommending. Here is the per-index rationale:\n\n---\n\n### LINEITEM (largest and most queried table)\n\n1. **`(l_shipdate, l_discount, l_quantity, l_extendedprice)`**\n   - Serves Q6 (shipdate range + discount + quantity filter) as an index-only scan: cost drops dramatically vs full scan. Also aids Q14 (shipdate range) and Q15 (suppkey-based aggregation over shipdate range).\n   - Confirmed cost: 36,258 for Q6.\n\n2. **`(l_orderkey, l_shipdate, l_extendedprice, l_discount)`**\n   - Serves Q3 (join on orderkey then filter l_shipdate > date), Q7 (orderkey join + shipdate range), Q8 (orderkey join).\n   - Enables index-only/index range scans for the inner side of nested loops on l_orderkey + l_shipdate.\n   - Confirmed cost: 169,732 for Q3.\n\n3. **`(l_orderkey, l_commitdate, l_receiptdate)`**\n   - Serves Q4 (semi-join checking l_commitdate < l_receiptdate), Q12 (date comparisons), Q21 (l3, l2 anti/semi joins on orderkey with commit/receipt date filters).\n   - Confirmed cost: 23,827 for Q4.\n\n4. **`(l_orderkey, l_returnflag, l_extendedprice, l_discount)`**\n   - Serves Q10: join on l_orderkey, filter l_returnflag='R', cover extendedprice and discount for the aggregation.\n   - Confirmed cost: 89,158 for Q10.\n\n5. **`(l_suppkey, l_orderkey, l_receiptdate, l_commitdate)`**\n   - Serves Q21: lookup by suppkey (from supplier), filter l_receiptdate > l_commitdate, retrieve orderkey.\n   - Confirmed cost: 43,014 for Q21 (slightly better than the 4-column variant).\n\n6. **`(l_partkey, l_suppkey, l_shipdate, l_quantity)`**\n   - Serves Q9 (join on l_partkey + l_suppkey to match partsupp, retrieve l_quantity for amount calc), Q20 (l_partkey + l_suppkey + l_shipdate range + quantity aggregation subquery).\n   - Confirmed cost: 72,789 for Q9; 98,062 for Q20.\n\n7. **`(l_partkey, l_shipinstruct, l_shipmode, l_quantity, l_extendedprice, l_discount)`**\n   - Serves Q19: join on l_partkey then immediately filter l_shipinstruct='DELIVER IN PERSON', enabling very selective index-only scan.\n   - Confirmed cost: 7,542 for Q19 (vs ~35,068 without this leading combination).\n\n8. **`(l_orderkey, l_quantity)`**\n   - Serves Q18: the subquery groups by l_orderkey and sums l_quantity to find orders with quantity > 312. Then the outer query also scans lineitem on l_orderkey.\n   - Confirmed cost: 419,988 for Q18 (index used for both subquery and outer join).\n\n9. **`(l_receiptdate, l_shipmode, l_orderkey, l_commitdate, l_shipdate)`**\n   - Serves Q12: filter l_receiptdate in range, then filter l_shipmode in ('RAIL','AIR'), l_commitdate < l_receiptdate, l_shipdate < l_commitdate.\n   - Confirmed cost: 78,310 for Q12.\n\n---\n\n### ORDERS\n\n10. **`(o_orderdate, o_custkey, o_orderkey, o_shippriority)`**\n    - Serves Q3 (o_orderdate < date filter, then join on o_custkey, return o_orderkey and o_shippriority), Q5 (o_orderdate range), Q8 (o_orderdate between range), Q10 (o_orderdate range + o_custkey join).\n    - Confirmed cost: 169,732 for Q3; widely reused across queries.\n\n11. **`(o_orderdate, o_orderpriority, o_orderkey)`**\n    - Serves Q4: filter o_orderdate in 3-month range, retrieve o_orderpriority and o_orderkey for semi-join with lineitem.\n    - Confirmed cost: 23,961 for Q4.\n\n12. **`(o_custkey, o_orderkey)`**\n    - Serves Q7 (join orders on o_custkey, retrieve o_orderkey), Q13 (left join on o_custkey), Q22 (anti-join checking o_custkey = c_custkey).\n    - Confirmed cost: Q7 used this index; Q22 used it in nested loop anti-join.\n\n13. **`(o_orderstatus, o_orderkey)`**\n    - Serves Q21: filter o_orderstatus='F' (roughly half the table), retrieve o_orderkey for hash join with lineitem.\n    - Confirmed cost: 43,014 for Q21.\n\n---\n\n### CUSTOMER\n\n14. **`(c_mktsegment, c_custkey)`**\n    - Serves Q3 (filter c_mktsegment='BUILDING', retrieve c_custkey for hash), Q13 (full customer scan but enables index-only on c_custkey).\n    - Confirmed cost: 171,922 for Q3 (used in both Q3 and Q13).\n\n15. **`(c_acctbal, c_custkey, c_phone)`**\n    - Serves Q22: filter c_acctbal > computed average (range scan), return c_custkey for anti-join and c_phone for substring check.\n    - Confirmed cost: 9,979 for Q22.\n\n---\n\n### PART\n\n16. **`(p_size, p_type, p_partkey, p_mfgr)`**\n    - Serves Q2 (filter p_size=21, then LIKE '%STEEL' on p_type; index-only scan) and Q16 (filter p_size IN list via bitmap index scan).\n    - Confirmed cost: 52,218 for Q2.\n\n17. **`(p_brand, p_type, p_size, p_partkey)`**\n    - Serves Q17 (filter p_brand='Brand#51', container filter, bitmap heap scan), Q19 (BitmapOr on brand+size conditions), Q16 (brand/type/size grouping).\n    - Confirmed cost: 14,783 for Q17; 7,542 for Q19; 39,413 for Q16.\n\n18. **`(p_name, p_partkey)`**\n    - Serves Q9 (p_name LIKE '%honeydew%' \u2014 even with the leading wildcard the index can help for index-only retrieval of p_partkey), Q20 (p_name LIKE 'burlywood%' \u2014 prefix match is especially efficient).\n    - Confirmed cost: 72,789 for Q9; 98,062 for Q20.\n\n---\n\n### PARTSUPP\n\n19. **`(ps_partkey, ps_suppkey, ps_supplycost)`**\n    - Serves Q2 subquery (lookup by ps_partkey, then join on ps_suppkey, retrieve ps_supplycost for MIN), Q9 (join on ps_partkey+ps_suppkey to get ps_supplycost), Q11 (join on ps_suppkey for nation filter), Q16 (index-only scan for ps_partkey+ps_suppkey), Q20 (lookup by ps_partkey).\n    - Confirmed cost: 52,218 for Q2; used heavily across Q9, Q11, Q16, Q20.\n\n20. **`(ps_suppkey, ps_partkey, ps_supplycost, ps_availqty)`**\n    - Serves Q2 outer query (join by ps_suppkey from supplier, retrieve ps_partkey, ps_supplycost for cost matching), Q11 (join on ps_suppkey, aggregate ps_supplycost * ps_availqty).\n    - Confirmed cost: 7,387 for Q11; used as index-only scan in Q2 outer loop.\n\n---\n\n### SUPPLIER\n\n21. **`(s_nationkey, s_suppkey)`**\n    - Serves Q2, Q5, Q7, Q8, Q9, Q10, Q11, Q20, Q21: all join supplier on s_nationkey (from nation) and retrieve s_suppkey, making this a universally beneficial index for the TPC-H star schema pattern.\n    - Confirmed: used in virtually every multi-table query as bitmap/index-only scan.\n\n---\n\n### Queries intentionally not targeted with dedicated indexes:\n- **Q1**: Filters ~97% of lineitem rows (l_shipdate \u2264 a late date). A covering index would be very large and the planner confirmed it prefers a parallel seq scan (cost ~230,000 unchanged). No beneficial index exists.\n- **Q15**: The CREATE VIEW syntax cannot be EXPLAIN-ed directly; however the underlying l_shipdate range + l_suppkey grouping is served by the `(l_shipdate, l_discount, l_quantity, l_extendedprice)` and `(l_suppkey, ...)` indexes already recommended.\n- **Q13**: Uses a NOT LIKE filter on o_comment which prevents index use; a seq scan is optimal. The c_custkey index helps the outer side.\n",
